              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Environmental Defense (the petitioner) argues that the agency may not adopt a new definition of \u201cmodification\u201d that differs from the one used under prior regulations."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. HUNGAR",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0001-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The petitioner\u2019s counsel, Mr. Hungar, says the regulation language does not support interpreting a change in hours of operation as a physical change."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0002-0012"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The agency\u2019s interpretation could lead to increased pollution because operating the plant 24 hours a day would double emissions compared with a 12\u2011hour schedule."
      }
    ],
